WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How are you?
-I'm good. How are you?

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Good. It's very lovely
to have you here.

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:05.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is not your first book.
-No.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:06.740 line:92%
-But what was the genesis,

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:09.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
and what set you off the pat
to write this book

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.811
about, really, the moment
we're living in right now?

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:15.515
-So, I really wanted to writ
something that was part memoir

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:18.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
but was also, I think,
encapsulating

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of what women have bee
going through right now,

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:21.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
especially
in the last few years,

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:25.759
since 2017's Me Too movement
and Time's Up and all of tha

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:30.163
and this sort of condensed sense
of palpable rage and chang

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.832
that feels uncontrollable
and really terrifying,

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:35.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
and to talk a lot about
leaning into that

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:35.969 line:92%
and not being afraid of it

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:38.405
and to know that the chang
that we're sort of seeking

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:41.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a culture and as a countr
and as individual genders

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:44.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
is going to come when
we are in our own discomfort

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:46.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we're not afraid
of it anymore.

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:47.347 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-One of the things that

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:49.349 size:78% position:39%
a paperback gives you
an opportunity to do

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:51.618
is add something, revise things.
-Yes.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:54.921
-In this case, you had an
afterword where it seems -

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:56.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess you wrote
six months ago --

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:59.993 size:84% position:42%
about the candidates
in the Democratic field

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.127 line:92%
and how important it was to have

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
sort of a diverse group
of candidates.

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:06.099
And basically,
just this idea of representation

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:08.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how that
can help avoid moments

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
like the one
we're living in now,

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you have
more voices in power.

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:14.240
-Yes. Well, statistically,
it's actually proven, too,

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, if you have more women
in positions of power,

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:20.180
if you have more equality
in positions of power,

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
sexual harassment
and sexual assault

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:23.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
actually goes down
in the workplace.

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:24.851 line:92%
That is a fact and a statistic

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:26.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think one
of the most important things

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:29.155 size:84% position:42%
we're seeing about --
not only this election,

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:29.856 size:81% position:41% line:92%
but the powerful women

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:32.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
like Ayanna Pressley
and Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:35.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, coming into powe
and coming into office,

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:38.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that we're actually seein
the living embodiment

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:41.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
of who we are
in those positions of power,

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:45.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
which allows us to feel like
we can capably become

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
those types women someday
in our own lives.

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:49.976
So I think it's so important
that what we're seeing right now

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:53.313
is a lot of different type
of women who are running.

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.380 size:88% position:44% line:92%
It keeps narrowing down.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
I myself
am a huge Elizabeth Warren fan

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.418 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I've endorsed her.

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think
she's absolutely incredible.

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:03.022
And what's so great about it
though, is that there's options,

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:04.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we didn't really
have that before.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:07.193
So now that we have the options,
we can actually talk about

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:11.798
the fundamental ideas and plan
behind who those candidates ar

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:12.499 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and why we want them.

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:15.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Another thing you did was
you wrote an epilogue,

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:17.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is a letter
to your daughter.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:18.204 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:20.640
-And I certainly felt this
as well, in this moment --

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
you describe in this era
we're living through,

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
where there's
a lot to be angry about

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:27.747 size:81% position:41%
and a lot of, I think,
reflecting on the way

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.449 line:92%
we treated different genders

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:30.583 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and having two boys --

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:31.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think about it all the time.
-Yeah.

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:35.188
-Has being a parent informed
the way you think about this

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:36.322 line:92%
and the way write about this

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:37.257 line:92%
-Oh, it's changed everything

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:39.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so many
of my girlfriends, too --

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:43.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I imagine, for you,
it must be a complex feeling

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:45.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
to have two sons
in this particular era

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.333 line:92%
with this particular president

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:49.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
just as anyone who has,
you know, girls,

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:50.170 size:75% position:38% line:92%
who's raising girls.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:53.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, for me, I think
one of the hardest things

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:54.841
that I had to come to grips with
as a parent

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:57.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
was that
I really couldn't control it

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I couldn't control
the outcome.

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:01.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I couldn't control
protecting them.

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:04.784
I couldn't control making them
better in certain instances.

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:06.352 size:75% position:38%
There's just so much
you can't control --

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:09.022 size:84% position:42%
and letting go of that,
but knowing you can be

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:11.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
the most empathic nurturer
and supporter

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
through the good and the bad
with your child

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:17.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
was something that was
a real harnessing moment for m

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.766
in getting to write that lette
to her at the end of the book.

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:22.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You talk about lacking contro
as a parent.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:25.471 size:81% position:41%
My wife had gave birth
in the lobby of our --

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
-Which was a --

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:29.842
you know, that was a perfect
example of a lack of control

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:31.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
Because...

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:33.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you could control it,
you wouldn't do that.

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:35.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:38.384 line:92%
-You had a similar labor issue

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:40.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was, again,
a lack of control.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:43.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I also refer to it
as a labor issue.

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:44.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yes.

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:46.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's what women call it
in the hospital.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:48.628 line:92%
"Sir, I'm having a labor issue!"

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:52.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
"Sir!"

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:55.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
I -- It was
actually like a day --

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:57.637 line:92%
the day after Trump had won,

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:58.838 line:92%
and I was coming up the stairs

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:00.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the subway
at Columbus Circle

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:03.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
and started
to feel contractions,

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:06.512
and I realized that I was
actually, like, going --

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
about to give birth
in the subway.

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:10.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-As I was coming up the stairs

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:11.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was really scary,
and there was --

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:13.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
all of these different thing
that -- happening,

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm including
a wonderful homeless man

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:18.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
who offered me an orange
to help.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:19.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
-Sure.

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:22.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was great,
and then, also, you know,

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:23.563 line:92%
offered to help give birth

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:25.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was
a very intense experience.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was, in my mind,
freaking out,

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:28.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I chronicled this
in the book.

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.270 size:84% position:42%
And I was just like,
"I don't know if I'm --

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:33.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, the depression
from Hillary Clinton losing,

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
is making my water break,

00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:36.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
or if I'm having, like,
a miscarriage

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:38.411 line:92%
because Trump has -- has won."

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:39.379 line:92%
I know that's really intense

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:40.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that's how it felt
in that moment.

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:41.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Chuckling ] Sure.
-Yeah.

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:44.117
And it actually just turned ou
I was having an anxiety attack

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:45.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
That's all it was --

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:47.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was just like
a huge anxiety attack.

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:47.820 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-There were a lot, yeah.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hospitals are filled of people
with doctors being like,

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:51.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Ma'am, you're not having
your baby right now."

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:52.692 line:92%
